CORE
read_after_increment.c
--div-by-zero-check --evaluation-order-check
^\[main\.evaluation-order\.\d+\] line 12 value of a\[.*tmp_post_i\] is independent of evaluation order: FAILURE$
^\[main\.division-by-zero\.\d+\] line 12 division by zero in 10 / a\[.*\]: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The read of a[i] (with the value of i before the increment) may happen before
or after the call to g, which sets a[0] from 0 to 1: reading a[0] before the
call would divide by zero. The read happens after i++, and its value is
checked to be the same at every point after i++ until the end of the full
expression. The division by zero is reported as this dependence on the
evaluation order, as the division itself is only evaluated at the end.
